WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:07.900
Give a young mammal extra nerve growth factor, and its sympathetic ganglia swell.

2
00:00:08.660 --> 00:00:13.180
Inject a newborn mouse with an anti -serum against it, and the ganglia waste away.

3
00:00:13.960 --> 00:00:15.500
Call the protein NGF.

4
00:00:16.220 --> 00:00:18.020
Results like these tempt a strong conclusion.

5
00:00:19.140 --> 00:00:22.300
Does NGF decide how many neurons an animal has?

6
00:00:23.133 --> 00:00:25.493
A small ganglion can mean two things.

7
00:00:26.073 --> 00:00:30.633
Either too few neurons were made, or the normal number was made and some were lost.

8
00:00:31.413 --> 00:00:35.613
In chick spinal ganglia, many neurons formed and grew fibres first.

9
00:00:36.753 --> 00:00:38.933
Dying cells became conspicuous later.

10
00:00:39.813 --> 00:00:41.173
Neurons are overproduced.

11
00:00:42.117 --> 00:00:45.257
The target is the tissue an axon grows to and connects with.

12
00:00:45.777 --> 00:00:48.397
It supplies the factor, and the amount is limited.

13
00:00:49.197 --> 00:00:51.137
Axons that reach the target take it up.

14
00:00:51.737 --> 00:00:54.257
Neurons that get too little die by apoptosis.

15
00:00:54.917 --> 00:00:58.257
The idea is that neurons compete for a limiting amount of factor.

16
00:00:58.837 --> 00:01:01.997
Most death should come as axons arrive, not before.

17
00:01:02.800 --> 00:01:04.320
An antiserum carries a doubt.

18
00:01:04.760 --> 00:01:08.060
It might kill neurons by binding something other than NGF.

19
00:01:08.780 --> 00:01:10.520
A knockout mouse settles it.

20
00:01:11.160 --> 00:01:16.200
Mice lacking a working TrkA, the receptor for NGF, still form the ganglion.

21
00:01:16.840 --> 00:01:19.620
Neurons are made and their axons start to grow as usual.

22
00:01:20.020 --> 00:01:24.600
But the sympathetic neurons are lost after embryonic day 15 .5.

23
00:01:25.160 --> 00:01:26.440
The neurons were produced.

24
00:01:26.880 --> 00:01:28.080
What failed was survival.

25
00:01:29.033 --> 00:01:32.093
Add excess NGF to a developing chick embryo.

26
00:01:32.713 --> 00:01:36.993
The ganglia get larger, mostly because more neurons escape the normal death.

27
00:01:37.633 --> 00:01:38.913
How would you know it is survival?

28
00:01:39.693 --> 00:01:43.593
You count neurons and dying cells, and you mark dividing cells.

29
00:01:44.293 --> 00:01:46.453
Early NGF can also drive division.

30
00:01:46.953 --> 00:01:51.593
No new neurons appear from survival alone, and none changes what kind of neuron it

31
00:01:51.593 --> 00:01:52.593
is.

32
00:01:52.617 --> 00:01:54.417
This gives a ceiling for survival.

33
00:01:55.117 --> 00:01:59.457
Neurons surviving equal the smaller of two numbers: the neurons made, and the

34
00:01:59.457 --> 00:02:00.977
neurons the factor can support.

35
00:02:01.557 --> 00:02:03.497
Extra factor raises the second number.

36
00:02:04.257 --> 00:02:06.077
Survival alone never raises the first.

37
00:02:06.537 --> 00:02:10.077
The ceiling holds for the population you measured, with its own factor.

38
00:02:10.677 --> 00:02:14.417
A survival factor can decide how many of the neurons made stay alive.

39
00:02:14.937 --> 00:02:17.177
It cannot add neurons that were never made.
